codex
The SDK contract itself looks mostly compatible: `system_`, top-level `cache_control`, and `tool_choice: { type: :auto/:none }` are accepted by the 1.68 API types, and the SDK’s content block params can round-trip thinking/tool_use/tool_result blocks. The larger risk I’m seeing is application control flow and data freshness rather than Ruby keyword naming.
