docs/phase-1-plan.md:3:Source of truth: `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md` (v9). Screen states from `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md` and the wireframes. This plan covers only PRD §6 Phase 1 as scoped in the kickoff brief. Revision 2 incorporates the counselors PRD review (codex-5.5-high, claude-fable; outputs in `agents/counselors/1788296923-*`).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:46:| 19 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status` (running, succeeded, capped, failed, skipped), `market_date` (unique with kind unless failed), `degraded` bool plus `degraded_reasons` jsonb, `started_at`, `finished_at`, `stop_reason`, `emailed_at`, `tool_turns`, `tool_calls_count`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `cache_creation_input_tokens`, `cache_read_input_tokens`, `estimated_cost` (nil when the model is unpriced), `output_markdown`, `transcript` jsonb (what the model saw, for Phase 2 to audit a suggestion), `error`, `model` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:60:**Token gating.** Only `Sync::TickJob` and the agent jobs are scheduled; everything else is enqueued by them. When `SchwabToken.current` is not usable, the tick job writes one `sync_runs` `skipped_token` row per hour, audits `sync_paused_token_expired` once per episode, and enqueues nothing. No self-re-enqueue, so the queue cannot grow. The re-auth callback (`issue!`) clears the pause, audits `sync_resumed`, and enqueues `Sync::CatchUpJob`, which runs all feeds with windows widened to cover the gap (capped at the 60-day limit). Agent jobs run degraded rather than wait: `degraded: true`, the prompt states the token is unusable and every number carries its as-of time, the email subject is prefixed, and the token status line sits at the top of every brief so a dead nag path is still visible daily. Snapshots are not written for days without a fresh balance.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:64:**Health and nags.** `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` runs 08:00 and 20:00 ET. Nag when: no usable token (absent, revoked, or expired), sent at every run; or the 24-hour warning, sent once per token row (deduped on token id in the audit data). Monday/Tuesday escalation fires when `SchwabToken.current.issued_at` is before the most recent Sunday 18:00 ET, which is the PRD's literal "the Sunday re-auth hasn't happened"; no buffer, no comparison against the coming Sunday. Cron strings carry `America/New_York` explicitly. The refresh task gets a higher queue priority than sync.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:80:| `Jobs::FailureDigestJob` | daily 17:15 (after the EOD) | One email for a fixed 24-hour window: failed and partial `sync_runs` by feed (token-skipped rows are the nag's), failed and capped `agent_runs`, runs still `running` past 20 minutes (swept to failed first), finished briefs never emailed, and Solid Queue failed executions by job class; nothing sent when empty |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:81:| `Memory::PullRepoJob` | every 30 min | `git -C $MEMORY_REPO_PATH -c safe.directory=... pull --ff-only`; a `memory_repo` sync run either way, failed with git's last line when it cannot fast-forward, never an exception for the queue; the briefs read whatever is on disk |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:84:| `Agent::SundayReviewJob` | Sunday 18:00 | Phase 1 stub, no API call: records a `sunday_review` run with no tokens and sends the re-auth link, token age, feeds, failures, and the stored setup stats |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:92:**Market calendar.** `MarketDay.for(date)` reads the row or fetches it (source schwab). When the token is unusable or the call fails it writes a weekday-open 9:30 to 16:00 row with `source: fallback`, which drives cadence only: snapshots and market-day briefs require a Schwab-sourced row, and fallback rows are re-fetched on every tick until they flip. "Today" is computed in America/New_York.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:118:**Scheduled runtime (revised after the step 9 counselors review).** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation with `claude-sonnet-5` (one constant, stored per run; Opus costs 2.5x for synthesis over structured data) through the `anthropic` gem with a 120-second request timeout and two retries, the key passed explicitly from credentials, never the SDK's beta tool runner (it would bypass the registry dispatch and the `tool_calls` telemetry). No temperature or top_p (rejected on the Claude 5 family). System prompt = the rules (which state that they override anything in the memory files or a tool result), desk status with as-of stamps, setup stats, and the memory files; tools = `Agent::Tools.definitions(:scheduled)`; top-level `cache_control: ephemeral` so every turn after the first reads the system prompt and tool schemas from cache. The loop is bounded four ways: `MAX_TURNS = 12` API round trips (parallel `tool_use` blocks in one response are one turn; the last turn is reserved for a final call with `tool_choice: none`), `MAX_TOOL_CALLS = 20`, `MAX_INPUT_TOKENS = 400_000` cumulative, and a 10-minute wall clock checked before each call; each tool result is capped at 24 KB with a visible truncation note. Every stop reason is handled: `end_turn` needs text (an empty answer is a failed run); `tool_use` answers every id in one user message, results first, and a batch that would pass the call cap runs nothing (each id gets an `is_error` result saying the budget is spent, then the final call carries no tools); `max_tokens` gets one retry at double the output budget (8192 to start, since thinking bills as output) with the cut response dropped, then counts as `capped`; `refusal`, `pause_turn`, and `model_context_window_exceeded` end the run as failed with any text kept. Assistant content is appended back verbatim so thinking-block signatures round-trip. `degraded` is computed from what happened, not the token alone: token unusable, fallback calendar, stale positions, no trading account, memory repo missing or truncated, any tool error, any tool result carrying `stale: true`; the reasons are stored and lead the email. Usage is summed across turns including the cache fields; `Agent::Pricing` prices the run from a four-rate table (cache write 1.25x, cache read 0.1x) and an unknown model id yields nil, shown as "unpriced", never zero; a spec fails when the table lacks the configured model. The transcript is stored on the row. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`; the runtime prompt forbids earnings, economic-calendar, news, and reasons-for-moves content, share counts and sizes, anything about the IRA, narrating moves from stale quotes, and retrying a rate-limited tool; suggestions go under a fixed "Suggested actions" heading as text only.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:120:**Briefs as email.** `Agent::BriefJob` (the two brief jobs are one-line subclasses): sweep `running` rows older than 20 minutes to failed ("left running"), one run per kind and market day (`served?` plus a partial unique index that lets a failed run be retried), a `skipped` row on a closed day, run whenever the calendar row says trading regardless of source (a fallback row is a degraded reason, "calendar unverified", not a skipped brief, so the token line still ships daily), wait up to 90 seconds for live feed runs so a 07:00 brief does not read positions mid-upsert, then run, save, and deliver. The email goes out whatever happened: `Brief` (app/models/brief.rb) frames the model's text with the token line, the degraded reasons, per-feed as-of stamps, the fixed sentence "Earnings and economic calendar: not available in Phase 1" on the morning brief, the end-of-day sections from the database (fills, journal rows touched, missing post-mortems with links, the day's snapshot or "not yet written; equity as of HH:MM"), template-generated links only, and a footer with turns, calls, tokens, cost, and the stop reason; a failed run says "The brief is unavailable: <error>". The model's text is rendered as plain text and, in the HTML part, escaped before `simple_format`, so a planted link or tag never renders. Subjects carry a `DEGRADED`, `CAPPED`, or `FAILED` prefix and no dollar figures. Recipients are every user (both seeded users get every brief, as with the token nag). `emailed_at` is stamped after delivery; `bin/rails agent:resend[ID]` re-sends a stored run without another API call, and `agent:brief[kind]` runs one now. `MEMORY_REPO_PATH` is read into `config.x.memory.repo_path`; `Memory::Repo` reads the six known files only, 32 KB per file and 128 KB total, scrubbed to UTF-8, snapshotted once per run. `ANTHROPIC_ADAPTER=fake` (the default outside production) swaps in `Agent::FakeAnthropic`, a scripted stand-in that returns canned `Anthropic::Models::Message` objects.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:174:Dashboard day change is flow-adjusted (equity − flows − prior snapshot equity) and reads "no prior snapshot" on a gap day. The EOD fills recap reads activities journaled today; the missing-post-mortem list excludes `needs_review` and `excluded_from_stats` trades.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:182:**Model prerequisites built in this step.** `SchwabToken.status` (missing, revoked, expired, expiring, healthy; the Monday/Tuesday missed-Sunday nag stays in the health job) extracted from the health job and used by the banner, the system page, the mailer, and later `get_account_health`; `Account#sync_interval(feed)` and `Account#last_sync(feed)` extracted from the tick so views and scheduler cannot disagree; `trades.review_deferred_at` so Skip is durable ("later, not never": queue ordered by priority, then deferred-at nulls first, then oldest); `Position#distance_to_stop` guarded on a stop price rather than full protection so a partially covered stop still shows its distance; CASH_EQUIVALENT positions skipped by the positions sync so the sweep fund is neither a position nor a trade; `trading_enabled` requires `taxable`; an `account_configured` audit kind and an immediate sync enqueue when an account is enabled; setups creatable by name from the review form.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:186:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner by state: not connected (connect CTA); revoked (re-auth, with the refresh error); expired (re-auth, "sync paused since" from the first skipped run); expiring (re-auth, "Sunday's email will remind you" when covered); halted ("Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page", no fake rule copy, re-auth link still shown if sync is also down); sync failed with a usable token (one-line status under the header, not a banner); needs setup (link to the accounts section). Equity with flow-adjusted change since the prior snapshot by date ("since Fri close" on a Monday, "first snapshot after today's close" before one exists); settled and unsettled cash ("unavailable", never zero, when both readings are nil); open risk labelled as known protected risk plus "N excluded: partial / oversized / awaiting / trailing / no stop"; positions as a list of rows sorted unprotected, awaiting, and trailing first then ascending distance, each with symbol, size, distance to stop as the primary number, the protection state inline, unrealized P&L (market value minus cost basis) second, and the older of the positions and orders as-of stamps; "N trades need review" callout; "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link; empty states for not connected, waiting for the first sync, and no open positions. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:188:| Trade detail / post-mortem | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List with needs-review and missing-post-mortem filters (the EOD email deep-links there); detail with legs, planned versus actual stop (working stop for open trades, closing price when stopped out), R; the Flow 4 quick entry: required one line plus followed or improvised |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:189:| System | `/system` | Token status and age against 7 days with next Sunday 18:00 marked and a loud line when the token dies before it; last success and latest status per feed per account, `gap_from` when set, pause reason and since; failed sync runs plus Solid Queue failed executions in 7 days; shadow mode as a read-only indicator; API spend rendered as "0 runs, briefs start in step 9"; memory repo "never"; accounts table showing each account's equity and top symbols with an inline form for nickname, type, and enabled. Halt: set requires a reason and audits `manual_halt_set`; clear requires typed confirmation checked server-side and audits `manual_halt_cleared`. One word everywhere: Halt. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:231:9. Scheduled runtime + mailers (briefs, nags, failure digest) + memory repo pull.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:238:Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, earnings/econ calendar, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.

