 succeeded in 0ms:
   200	
   201	## 8. Testing
   202	
   203	- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
   204	- **VCR cassettes** in `spec/cassettes`, recorded against Schwab only once the app is Ready For Use, with a scrubber that replaces bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and account hash values before write. Until then, cassettes are hand-built from community-client response shapes and marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
   205	- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
   206	- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): a scenarios route drawn only under `Rails.env.test?` and guarded again in the controller with `Schwab.fake?`, which resets the fake client, seeds with the factories (never by driving jobs), and signs in a seeded user by setting the session cookie because there is no inbox to read a magic link from. Times are relative: fresh is now, stale is three hours ago, expiring is 22 hours out, expired is two days ago. Scenarios: healthy, expiring, expired, halted, not connected, needs setup, one unprotected position, a failed sync with a usable token, the review queue with Skip persisting across reload, the post-mortem save, and re-auth success and failure (the seeded hash must match the fake's). The MCP endpoint is covered by request specs, not Playwright. The Playwright server runs with the test queue adapter.
   207	- **`bin/ci`**: Rails 8.1 `ActiveSupport::ContinuousIntegration` with steps in `config/ci.rb`, the pattern borrowed from Patchvault. Kickoff order: rubocop → rspec → brakeman (strict, warnings fail) → `bin/importmap audit` → `bundle exec bundle-audit check --update` → Playwright (`bin/playwright`, which boots a test-env server with the FakeClient, runs `npx playwright test`, and tears down). Fails on the first red step.
   208	
   209	---
   210	
   211	## 9. Deploy
   212	
   213	- `Procfile`: `web: bundle exec puma -C config/puma.rb`, `worker: bin/jobs`, `release: bin/rails db:prepare`. One Postgres 17 service and one database: Solid Queue, Solid Cache, and Solid Cable tables live in the primary schema (migration `InstallSolidTables`), so `db:prepare` on `DATABASE_URL` is the whole database setup.
   214	- `app.json` for the release phase.
   215	- `bin/dokku-setup`: documents postgres plugin, letsencrypt, config vars (`RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, `MEMORY_REPO_PATH`), the storage mount for the memory repo (a clone on the host owned by uid 1000 so the container's `git pull --ff-only` can write `.git`; the runtime image carries git; if the remote needs a deploy key, a host cron doing the pull is the alternative and the job then only records what it finds), `ps:scale worker=1`, and the daily offsite DB dump from PRD §5.9 (postgres plugin backup to object storage on a cron).
   216	- `nginx.conf.d/mcp.conf` (or `dokku nginx:set client-max-body-size`): a small `client_max_body_size` (1 MiB) so the MCP body cap does not depend on Rails having already parsed the JSON for its log line.
   217	- App time zone `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`; Solid Queue recurring schedules use the same.
   218	
   219	---
   220	
   221	## 10. Build order (green `bin/ci` at each step)
   222	
   223	1. Tooling: RSpec, rubocop config, brakeman, bundler-audit, `bin/ci` (without Playwright), authentication generator adapted to magic link, AR encryption keys, credentials layout, crest in the layout.
   224	2. Migrations 1–21, models with validations/enums, `AuditEvent` append-only trigger, `SystemSettings` singleton.
   225	3. Schwab adapter: `Schwab::Client` (OAuth, accounts, positions, orders, transactions, market hours, quotes, price history) with retry/backoff/limiter, `Schwab::FakeClient`, response mappers, `docs/verify-on-approval.md` started from §12.
   226	4. OAuth controller + token model + refresh job + token health job + re-auth pages + pause/catch-up + audit events.
   227	5. Sync jobs, market calendar, tick scheduler, `sync_runs`, working-stop detection.
   228	6. Journal builder (bootstrap, link, review path) + setup stats + snapshots.
   229	7. Dashboard, system health, trade screens; Playwright added to `bin/ci`.
   230	8. MCP server + tool registry with permission metadata (decision 0.8 verified 2026-09-01: the connector dialog offers a request header).
   231	9. Scheduled runtime + mailers (briefs, nags, failure digest) + memory repo pull.
   232	10. Seeds for dev via FakeClient; `Procfile`, `app.json`, `bin/dokku-setup`; DHH-skill review pass.
   233	
   234	---
   235	
   236	## 11. Explicitly not built in Phase 1
   237	
   238	Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, earnings/econ calendar, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.
   239	
   240	---
   241	
   242	## 12. Schwab assumptions to verify on approval
   243	
   244	Maintained in `docs/verify-on-approval.md` (30 items as of the step 3 contract review). The original seed list:
   245	
   246	From PRD §9: exact `TaxLotMethod` enum values; order-endpoint rate limits. Added by this plan:
   247	- `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions` returns balances in the same payload (`currentBalances`, `initialBalances`).
   248	- Which balance fields map to settled cash vs unsettled cash for a cash account.
   249	- Orders endpoint supports `fromEnteredTime`/`toEnteredTime` and a `status` filter; maximum lookback window.
   250	- Transactions endpoint: 60-day start-date limit, `activityId` uniqueness, `orderId` presence on trade activities, transfer-item structure with fee items, CUSIP presence on every instrument (cash equivalents, sweeps, options).
   251	- Corporate-action activity shapes for splits, mergers, spin-offs, return of capital, and whether old and new CUSIPs arrive in one activity.
   252	- Market-hours endpoint takes one date per call and returns pre/regular/post session times.
   253	- Order status enum values for "working" stops; cancel/replace produces a new order id and marks the old one REPLACED.
   254	- Fractional-share quantities in positions and orders.
   255	- Refresh token expiry is 7 days from issuance and is not extended by access-token refreshes.
   256	- Claude app custom connectors: static bearer header availability for this org (decision 0.8).
   257	
   258	---
   259	
   260	## 13. Working method, per phase and per build step
   261	
   262	Each numbered step in §10 that ships a feature runs this loop:
   263	
   264	1. **PRD review with counselors** (`counselors run`, agents `codex-5.5-high` and `claude-fable`): the relevant PRD sections plus this plan's section for the step. Findings are folded into the plan before code.
   265	2. **Build** the feature vertically per §10.
   266	3. **RSpec green** and reviewed for coverage against the §8 priority list, not just passing.
   267	4. **DHH skill review pass** (`dhh-code-reviewer` agent) on the step's diff; fix what it flags.
   268	5. **Counselors review of the build** (same two agents) on the diff; fix or explicitly decline each finding in the commit message.
   269	6. **`bin/ci` green.** Commit.
   270	
   271	Counselors runs are long (10 to 20 minutes) and run in the background while unrelated work continues. Whole-phase gates: the counselors PRD review before step 1 (done, revision 2 of this plan is the result), and a DHH pass plus counselors review over the full Phase 1 diff after step 10.

